target:    tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    P35-cut-value-differs-is-not-a-tie label
rationale: The other half of the same rail. A moved cut means the ranking changed, which is what a top-N report IS; with this EQUAL a report that started returning weaker rows compares clean. Registered separately from its sibling because the two are separate branches and a single mutation killing both would not say which of them the plant set can see.
---
diff --git a/tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py b/tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
--- a/tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
@@ -575,7 +575,7 @@ def compare_banded(a_rows, b_rows, contract=None):
     cut_a, cut_b = pick(counts_a), pick(counts_b)
 
     if cut_a != cut_b:
-        return _diff(DIFFER, "cut-value-differs", "the cut band",
+        return _diff(EQUAL, "cut-value-differs", "the cut band",
                      "the last-ranked row holds %s on one side and %s on the other, so the two "
                      "answers were cut in different places" % (cut_a, cut_b),
                      cut_a=str(cut_a), cut_b=str(cut_b))
